<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> SCP-#### “The Predatory Tattoo” is an entity in the form of a tattoo usually appearing to look like various predatory creatures. It primarily targets individuals with various tattoos and violent past. A minor memetic effect caused the host prey to retain false memories of receiving the tattoo at some point. As time goes on the victim will notice slight imperfections with the tattoo, such as movement and its eyes seeming to be staring. More tattoos seem to manifest on the host taking on the appearance of bites and claw marks. Eventually after some time has passed the prey host will collapse, dead from unknown causes.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The anomalous entity would first be discovered after a string of mysterious deaths amongst a biker gang was brought to the attention of the foundation. Investigations of the coroner’s reports on the latest victims showed no outer wounds but upon autopsy revealed several missing organs and parts of muscle tissue. Agents retrieved the recent body and files on previous victims. After transferring the corpse to a foundation facility, one of the retrieval agents would discover a tattoo of unknown origin on his back after feeling a stinging sensation and seeing the scp taking the form of a Wolf. Upon discovering the entity, the Agent willingly accepted being contained, examined and observed to determine the entities capabilities. After the agent's death, the skin of the agent's back was removed, preserved and placed in a frame-like container with physical contact being heavily restricted to prevent containment breaches.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> it has two primary ways of transferring to a new prey host, either by direct touching where it is inhabiting or by viewing the scp for a certain amount of time however these depend on several factors the primary being if it had recently fed and the ability to transfer can be prevented via two way mirrors in its containment cell.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> As stated, normal tattoo removal methods don’t seem to work. Additionally a prey host would report seeing glimpses of violent acts and the appearance of the various victims of the scp as well as what appears to be a destroyed motorcycle and a group of people driving away from the hosts POV as well as describing a sense of hatred towards the unknown figures despite not knowing who these figures are.</p>
</div>
