			<div class="content" id="post-content-4861535">
									

<p>With the changes to the narrative made, yes, I'm comfortable with giving you a tentative <span style="color: green"><strong>greenlight</strong></span>. Potential for body horror here if you focus on a story of violence and vengeance for the victims.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>After transferring the corpse to a foundation facility, one of the retrieval agents would discover a tattoo of unknown origin on his back after feeling a stinging sensation and seeing the scp taking the form of a Wolf as well as a few dozen tattoo-like claw marks surrounding the main tattoo.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Keep that theme in mind when you write the rest of these portions. If the agent is also afflicted, for example, does it suggest that he/she too is a &quot;violent&quot; person? If so, how will you reveal these portions of their backstories so the readers can connect the dots?</p>
<p>Looking forward to reading the draft once you get your second greenlight! All the best!</p>

